{"type": "FeatureCollection", "metadata": {"note": "Yes -- Lansing, Michigan's state capital, had rail service well before 1900. Its first line arrived in 1856 (Detroit and Milwaukee Railroad), and by the early 1900s six separate railroads converged there. This feature traces one specific, well-documented line: the Jackson, Lansing and Saginaw Railroad (the 'Ramshorn Road', incorporated 1857 as the Amboy, Lansing and Traverse Bay Railroad), which reached Lansing from Owosso before 1861, opened Lansing-Owosso in November 1862, and was completed Jackson-Lansing-Owosso-Saginaw-Bay City by 1867 -- directly joining the existing Michigan Central Detroit-Chicago main line at Jackson (see michigan_central_detroit_chicago.geojson). Michigan Central leased it in 1871 and bought it outright in 1872. Geometry replaced 2026-08-24. The earlier version traced Owosso-Saginaw over the wrong corridor -- east to Durand and Flint and up from there, rather than the JL&S's own alignment north through St. Charles -- and drew Lansing-Owosso and Saginaw-Bay City as straight lines, coming out at 202.4 km against a documented Jackson-Bay City distance of about 115 miles (185 km). It now traces 185.2 km (115.1 miles) on the JL&S's own alignment throughout. Lansing-Owosso is assembled from the abandoned ex-Penn Central right of way through Bath and Laingsburg, with the largest bridged gap 3.8 km and a 1.8 km link into Lansing where the two sources do not meet; Saginaw-Bay City is now real geometry. The line's northern continuation, Bay City to Mackinaw City, is in michigan_central_michigan_network.geojson.", "sources": ["https://railroadfan.com/phpbb/viewtopic.php?t=30260 (Jackson, Lansing and Saginaw Railroad: incorporated 1857 as the Amboy, Lansing and Traverse Bay RR ('Ramshorn Road'); ~20 miles Owosso-Lansing completed before 1861; Lansing-Owosso opened Nov 1862; full Jackson-Owosso-Saginaw/Bay City line completed 1867; leased by Michigan Central 1871, sold to Michigan Central 1872; consolidated into Michigan Central 1916; abandoned under Conrail 1977)", "https://michiganrailroads.com/timeline/472-1900-1909/3625-timeline-1900 (by the early 1900s Lansing had six separate rail lines; Detroit & Milwaukee RR first reached Lansing in 1856; Michigan Central in 1872; Chicago & Grand Trunk in 1879; Michigan Central and Pere Marquette opened a joint Union Station in Lansing June 25 1902; Grand Trunk Western opened its own depot Jan 20 1903)"], "not_yet_sourced": "Exact frequency/timetable for any era; the routes of Lansing's other five ca.-1900 rail connections (only the Michigan Central/Jackson-Lansing-Saginaw line is depicted here).", "geometry_sources": ["OpenStreetMap (via Overpass API), railway=rail ways tagged usage=main or usage=branch, for the Jackson-Lansing and Owosso-Saginaw stretches", "Wikimedia Commons Data:Michigan Central Railroad.map (CC BY 4.0), derived from OpenStreetMap: the 'Jackson, Lansing and Saginaw Railroad' LineStrings, split at Bay City and used for Jackson-Lansing and Owosso-Bay City.", "OpenStreetMap via Overpass (maps.mail.ru mirror, 2026-08-24) for Lansing-Owosso: railway=abandoned ways tagged old_railway_operator/name 'Penn Central' -- the ex-NYC, ex-Michigan Central, ex-JL&S right of way -- chained by shortest path with straight-line links where fragments do not touch (largest 3.8 km)."], "line_label_audit": "2026-08-24: line labels normalised repo-wide to \"<operating company>: <line name>\" -- the company's common display name (legal suffixes dropped), then the line as a passenger would have known it, or its two terminals where the line carried no advertised name. Long intermediate station lists were reduced to endpoints. For features spanning several operators the company shown is the one that ran the line for most of its drawn years. See CLAUDE.md Rule 6."}, "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Michigan Central Railroad", "line": "Michigan Central: Saginaw Division", "id": "michigan-central-lansing-saginaw", "color": "#6A4C93", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 45, "speed_source": "estimated: Michigan Central branch-line steam/diesel service; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1862, "end": 1872, "headway_min": 720, "note": "Jackson, Lansing and Saginaw Railroad (independent); Lansing-Owosso opened Nov 1862, full Jackson-Saginaw/Bay City line by 1867; frequency estimated, unsourced", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://railroadfan.com/phpbb/viewtopic.php?t=30260", "https://michiganrailroads.com/timeline/472-1900-1909/3625-timeline-1900"]}, {"start": 1872, "end": 1916, "headway_min": 480, "note": "Purchased by Michigan Central 1872 (leased since 1871), operated as its Saginaw Division; frequency estimated, unsourced", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://railroadfan.com/phpbb/viewtopic.php?t=30260", "https://michiganrailroads.com/timeline/472-1900-1909/3625-timeline-1900"]}, {"start": 1916, "end": 1968, "headway_min": 360, "note": "Formally consolidated into Michigan Central 1916; frequency estimated, unsourced", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://railroadfan.com/phpbb/viewtopic.php?t=30260", "https://michiganrailroads.com/timeline/472-1900-1909/3625-timeline-1900"]}, {"start": 1976, "end": 1977, "headway_min": 360, "note": "Conrail from April 1 1976; the line was abandoned in 1977; frequency estimated, unsourced", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://railroadfan.com/phpbb/viewtopic.php?t=30260", "https://michiganrailroads.com/timeline/472-1900-1909/3625-timeline-1900"]}]}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-84.40324, 42.24877], [-84.40345, 42.24885], [-84.40439, 42.24915], [-84.4056, 42.2495], [-84.40588, 42.24959], [-84.40604, 42.24964], [-84.40625, 42.24975], [-84.40647, 42.24989], [-84.40669, 42.25006], [-84.40686, 42.2502], [-84.40701, 42.25034], [-84.40713, 42.2505], [-84.40726, 42.25068], [-84.40735, 42.25087], [-84.40745, 42.25116], [-84.4075, 42.25145], [-84.40751, 42.25165], [-84.40748, 42.25184], [-84.40719, 42.25282], [-84.40714, 42.25306], [-84.40712, 42.25333], [-84.40725, 42.25473], [-84.40746, 42.25589], [-84.4075, 42.25622], [-84.4075, 42.25665], [-84.40748, 42.25761], [-84.40754, 42.25831], [-84.40762, 42.25898], [-84.40763, 42.25905], [-84.40793, 42.26205], [-84.40795, 42.26253], [-84.40793, 42.26298], [-84.40786, 42.26373], [-84.40774, 42.26507], [-84.40765, 42.26618], [-84.40724, 42.27059], [-84.40722, 42.27111], [-84.40723, 42.2716], [-84.4073, 42.27202], [-84.40737, 42.27234], [-84.40752, 42.27286], [-84.40777, 42.27359], [-84.40815, 42.27454], [-84.40837, 42.2751], [-84.40866, 42.27559], [-84.40902, 42.27608], [-84.40958, 42.27672], [-84.40976, 42.27691], [-84.41048, 42.27769], [-84.41096, 42.2783], [-84.41145, 42.27903], [-84.41365, 42.28258], [-84.41414, 42.28332], [-84.41908, 42.29112], [-84.42072, 42.29371], [-84.42111, 42.2944], [-84.42127, 42.29476], [-84.42137, 42.29509], [-84.42149, 42.29559], [-84.4216, 42.29639], [-84.42172, 42.29865], [-84.42193, 42.30204], [-84.42197, 42.30311], [-84.42204, 42.30377], [-84.42206, 42.30394], [-84.4222